From 3e13e195554c0937d41e5d7da6a7b3a76c780152 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 00:07:30 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 12/14] Show a stereo document per eye with the stereo layer's
 Enable 3D
Forwarded: no, Krita's README sets a moratorium on AI-assisted contributions; carried in the edition's fork,
 https://invent.kde.org/danielcamposramos/krita

The "Stereo 3D" canvas showed one half of a side-by-side pair (the
image's view cut to one eye's picture), took the pair from the
document's shape or keywords, was off by default, read at start-up,
and needed "Paint on the Right View" to choose the half that strokes
land on.

The canvas now shows each eye its own picture of a stereo document, at
the image's size and in its coordinates, so every tool works where it is
used:
- a picture packed side by side or top and bottom shows each eye's view
  in both halves: each eye has textures of its own, made like the image's
  and fed from a paint device that holds the eye's view, copied from the
  projection into both halves, so its picture is what a 2D document of
  that view shows, and the texture filter never reaches the other eye's
  view at the seam or at the image's edges;
- a document with the top-level layers "Left eye" and "Right eye" shows
  each eye its layer, through textures of its own fed from the layer's
  projection.
The two pictures go to the canvas layer below the window as before, and
the decorations and the brush outline stay on the screen plane.

What a document is comes from its eye layers, else from the stereo
layer's policy for its file (libstereo-layer, Stereo::Picture): the
file's mark, the person's choice for that file kept in the shared
per-file store, then the shape of an unmarked picture. The View menu
offers the program's 3D options only: Enable 3D (the layer's own action,
on in every new window, for the window and the session), 3D Input Format
(the layer's menu of every packing a still can hold, for the document's
file) and Display Settings (kcmshell6 kcm_kscreen). Under a Wayland
compositor Krita takes the native Wayland platform whatever the surface
depth, and the main window is made for the canvas layer from the start.

Where the pair cannot be shown (Krita on X11, the canvas on OpenGL ES or
on Krita's QPainter canvas, wrap-around mode, a stereo surface the
graphics stack refuses) the canvas shows the left eye, says why on the
canvas and in the log, and puts the reason in Enable 3D's tooltip.

